{"type":"message","id":"d5707afd","parentId":"6b0a0af6","timestamp":"2026-04-06T05:45:19.439Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Docker is running but there's a 500 error on the Docker Desktop Linux engine. Let me check if Docker Desktop is running and what environment variables are set. I can see that locale is not available on Windows, and the LANG variable is empty.\n\nFor Docker Desktop on Windows, the CLI itself doesn't have a built-in Chinese translation. The Docker Dashboard (GUI) might support Chinese if the system is in Chinese. But the command-line tools (docker CLI) are not localized.\n\nHowever, what I can do is:\n1. Check if there's a DOCKER_CONFIG or other environment variable that can be set\n2. For Docker Desktop on Windows, the UI language depends on the system UI language\n\n\n3. The docker CLI itself doesn't support changing language - it's determined by the build\n\nSo the real answer is that Docker CLI doesn't have a language setting, but Docker Desktop on Windows will display in Chinese if the system language is set to Chinese. Let me check what the system language is.","thinkingSignature":"14ca5bb1b1544b0136b05f5154c60dd62c7e7b42083db78724023a7390369bd2"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_obg0zjinvwos_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"docker version --format '{{.Server.Version}}' 2>&1; echo \"---\"; systeminfo 2>&1 | findstr /i \"os\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":875,"output":255,"cacheRead":32834,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":33964,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775454308855,"responseId":"06227b64169372f7b597c3e66534e9fa"}}
