{"type":"message","id":"3e188124","parentId":"7c5eb5ab","timestamp":"2026-04-06T05:46:05.407Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The system locale is already zh-CN (Chinese). So Docker Desktop should already be in Chinese if it's configured properly.\n\nThe issue is that Docker CLI itself (the `docker` command) doesn't have built-in localization. It's a CLI tool whose messages are in English. The Docker Desktop GUI app might have some localization but it's limited.\n\nFor Docker CLI, there really isn't a way to \"汉化\" it since it doesn't have translation files. Docker Desktop as an app might show some Chinese if the Windows UI language is Chinese, but the actual `docker` command output is always in English.\n\nHowever, there might be third-party wrappers or scripts that translate docker output. \n\nI should be straightforward with the user: the docker CLI itself can't be localized since it lacks translation support, but if they're specifically referring to Docker Desktop's GUI interface, it should already display in Chinese given their system locale is zh-CN. The server errors they're seeing aren't actually translation issues—they're indicating Docker Desktop is having trouble connecting to its Linux engine.","thinkingSignature":"31dff02d6d314f35dbb98a5769ac0a0ef86ef9f58ed4a04da42e7997d138f2e3"},{"type":"text","text":"Docker CLI 本身是没有多语言支持的，输出是纯英文，没有内置的翻译文件。Docker Desktop 的 GUI 界面理论上应该已经跟随系统语言（你的系统已经是 zh-CN 中文）。\n\n不过我注意到你之前 `docker version` 的报错里有个 **500 Internal Server Error**，说明 Docker Desktop 本身可能没正常运行起来——这个才是首先要解决的。\n\n先检查一下 Docker Desktop 状态：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_mcj8vweyf0jz_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"docker info 2>&1 | Select-Object -First 20","timeout":15}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":1429,"output":333,"cacheRead":32834,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":34596,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total"