{"type":"message","id":"adb92838","parentId":"fcd92ea1","timestamp":"2026-04-06T05:46:40.887Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_967jz2x2xlf4_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Name              Id HasExited StartTime        \r\n----              -- --------- ---------        \r\nDocker Desktop 13392     False 2026/4/6 13:43:50\r\nDocker Desktop 26128     False 2026/4/6 13:43:51\r\nDocker Desktop 28492     False 2026/4/6 13:43:51\n\n(Command exited with code 1)"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":1,"durationMs":296,"aggregated":"Name              Id HasExited StartTime        \r\n----              -- --------- ---------        \r\nDocker Desktop 13392     False 2026/4/6 13:43:50\r\nDocker Desktop 26128     False 2026/4/6 13:43:51\r\nDocker Desktop 28492     False 2026/4/6 13:43:51\n\n(Command exited with code 1)","cwd":"C:\\Users\\zhang\\.openclaw\\workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1775454400885}}
{"type":"message","id":"79321079","parentId":"adb92838","timestamp":"2026-04-06T05:46:53.252Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Docker Desktop is running (multiple processes). The issue might be that the Docker Engine (Linux) inside Docker Desktop is having issues. The 500 error earlier suggests the backend isn't working properly.\n\nBut let me refocus - the user asked to \"汉化\" Docker. The core issue is that:\n1. Docker CLI doesn't have a language setting - it's English-only\n2. Docker Desktop GUI on Windows might show Chinese if Windows UI language is Chinese\n3. There are no translation packs available\n\nBut wait - maybe the user just wants the Docker Desktop UI to be in Chinese. Since their system is already zh-CN, Docker Desktop should already be in Chinese. But it might be showing English because of some setting.\n\n\nThe Windows system locale is already set to Chinese (zh-CN), so Docker Desktop should display in Chinese automatically. Since it's still showing English, I should explain that Docker CLI can't be localized but the Docker Desktop GUI should respect the system language setting. If they're still seeing English in the Docker Desktop interface, they might need to restart it or check if there's a specific language setting within the app itself.","thinkingSignature":"31d2f5c0e9473a7e4cbfa458a8e57fdc5015fc1a0492ce9d03071daeb6bd7b71"},{"type":"text","text":"Docker Desktop 已经在运行了，而且你的系统语言也是中文（zh-CN）。\n\n**关于\"汉化\"：**\n\n- **Docker CLI**（`docker run`、`docker ps` 等命令）本身是纯英文的，官方没有提供任何语言包或翻译文件，无法修改。\n- **Docker Desktop 图形界面**理论上应该跟随 Windows 系统语言——你的系统已经是中文，理论上 Docker Desktop 也应该是中文界面。\n\n如果你的 Docker Desktop 界面现在还是英文，可能需要重启一下：\n\n```\nDocker Desktop → 右下角托盘图标 → 右键 → Restart\n```\n\n重启后再看一下界面是不是已经变成中文了。\n\n---\n\n另外你之前 `docker version` 的报错是 **500 Internal Server Error**，说明 Docker 引擎没正常响应。重启 Docker Desktop 能顺便解决这个问题，一举两得。"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":2189,